===Argentina vs England===
{{see also|Argentina–England football rivalry}}
Argentina decided to use their change kit, feeling that it had granted them luck in the [[Argentina v England (1986 FIFA World Cup)|1986 World Cup quarter-final between the two sides]].<ref>{{cite news |last= Aguilar |first= Francesc |date=1 July 1998 |title= La camiseta reserva de Argentina les da suerte |trans-title= Argentina's reserve kit grants them luck |url= http://hemeroteca.mundodeportivo.com/preview/1998/07/01/pagina-11/395964/pdf.html |language=Spanish |work= [[Mundo Deportivo]] |access-date= 30 March 2021}}</ref> All four goals were scored in the first half, making it the first match in the tournament with as many goals scored before half-time.<ref>{{cite news |last= Perearnau |first= Francesc |date= 1 July 1998 |title= 'Chico picante' |trans-title= 'Spice Boy' |url= http://hemeroteca.mundodeportivo.com/preview/1998/07/01/pagina-11/395964/pdf.html |language= Spanish |work= [[Mundo Deportivo]] |location= |access-date= 30 March 2021}}</ref> With the score tied at 2–2, [[David Beckham]] retaliated after being fouled by [[Diego Simeone]] and was sent off. Beckham's teammate [[Michael Owen]] subsequently described Beckham's act as "childish and unnecessary", although Owen also said that the burnings of effigies of Beckham were undeserved.<ref>{{cite web |title=Michael Owen still resents David Beckham for 'letting England down' at World Cup vs Argentina |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/michael-owen-david-beckham-england-world-cup-argentina-alan-shearer-a9091166.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/michael-owen-david-beckham-england-world-cup-argentina-alan-shearer-a9091166.html |archive-date=1 May 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |website=The Independent [London] |access-date=18 June 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref> In the subsequent penalty shoot-out, Argentina went first. [[David Seaman]] saved Argentina's second penalty from [[Hernán Crespo]] to give England the advantage, but that was immediately cancelled when [[Carlos Roa]] saved from [[Paul Ince]]. The tie ended with another Roa save, from [[David Batty]]. Batty said it was the first penalty he had ever taken.<ref>{{cite web |title=Infamous Penalty Misses For England |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/60207-infamous-penalty-misses-for-england |website=Bleacher Report |access-date=18 June 2020}}</ref> England had also exited on penalties in the recent [[UEFA Euro 1996]] two years prior.

